From e3ed17835d1817d61601e996f7dd3253211e86bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:25:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Generic OpenID Connect login (authorization code + PKCE),
 configured by OIDC_* env

Own implementation for the Community Edition, comparable to the generic OIDC
patch in Cal.diy-Docker. It neither uses nor unlocks DocuSeal Pro (SAML) code
and needs no new gems (jwt and faraday ship with DocuSeal). Inactive without
OIDC_ISSUER/OIDC_CLIENT_ID/OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET.

- button on the login page (OIDC_BUTTON_LABEL)
- users are matched by verified e-mail and bound to the IdP subject
- new users only for members of OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS; users that lost the group
  are archived on their next attempt and reactivated when they are back
- SSO-linked users cannot use password login or password reset (MFA stays
  with the IdP), unless OIDC_ALLOW_PASSWORD_FOR_SSO_USERS=true
- the account-wide 2FA requirement applies to password logins only
- signing links for external signers are not affected
